-- Spellstorm's six levels, one biome each, in the order a run plays them
-- (Arena.BIOMES). How a level is laid out from these (paths, walls, props,
-- water) is Rust in sim/src/level.rs. Colours are sRGB { r, g, b }, as the
-- Godot game wrote them. This file hot-reloads: a changed biome applies to
-- the next level built (colours and light may change at once). Adding,
-- removing or reordering biomes takes effect at the next start.
--
-- Fields:
--   id, name          id and the name on screen
--   zones             the props of each of the three zones along the level
--   props, outside    props laid about the level and outside its walls
--   wall_props, water_props, wall_every (m between wall props)
--   enemies           { kind, how many go in a wave's pool } (monsters.luau)
--   boss              the boss kind at the end
--   fields            elements laid as permanent fields, a set every 9 m
--   floor_a, floor_b, tiles, wet, moss, moss_c, wall, fog, ambient, moon,
--   moon_energy, mist, mist_c, path_style, path_a, path_b
--   nave              a built biome with a straight middle stretch
--   corridor, isles, low_walls, outside_lava
--   wall_style        masonry, ossuary, rock, castle or cliff
--   density           how full of props the level is
